+# Server repair status — 20 October 2026 UTC
+
+## Current repair
+This supersedes the earlier same-day report. SDK 0.8.54 supports conditional updateMany with MongoDB query/update operators. The previous statement that conditional writes were unavailable was incorrect.
+
+- Server-priced, authorized checkout now serializes commerce mutations through one durable CommerceControl record. Stock reservations use conditional quantity decrements and order markers; coupon reservations also use conditional writes.
+- Card checkout claims an order before creating a provider session. Retries reuse a stored redirect; an uncertain provider failure cannot construct another session automatically. Signed settlement validates amounts and updates existing fulfillments.
+- Wallet payments use ledger balances under the commerce gate. Competing debits cannot spend the same funds through this service.
+- Withdrawals reserve funds with pending debits and stable request IDs. Rejection reverses the original hold. Administrator settlement requires confirmation and a reference for an external transfer already performed; it does not send money.
+- Card and wallet settlement allocate invoice numbers under the same gate.
+- Authorized cancellation releases marked stock and coupon reservations, reverses pending credits and cancels fulfillments once. Claimed card sessions and paid/preparing orders cannot use this automatic cancellation.
+- Unclaimed card/wallet orders have a 30-minute expiry. The admin-only expiry operation is connected to processWorkflowQueue; an actual automation schedule has not been verified.
+- Prior server pricing, guest credentials, order privacy, restricted entity writes, payout eligibility and privacy-request authorization fixes remain.
+
+## Verification
+63 tests pass. Frontend and commerce TypeScript checks, lint and production build pass.
+Tests cover authorization, forged totals, duplicate/replayed requests, concurrent wallet debits and withdrawals, card construction/reuse, partial writes, stock cancellation, expiry, settlement and privacy gates.
+
+Live isolated technical-record probes each sent 24 competing requests:
+- conditional idle-to-running claim: one winner, 23 losers;
+- conditional quantity decrement from one: one winner, 23 losers, zero errors.
+The temporary probe record and function source were removed afterward. No customer record, real payment, payout or outbound email was used in these checks.
+
+Live malformed checkout returned 400 Unknown order; invalid webhook signature returned 401. These establish routing and rejection behavior, not successful real payment processing.
+
+## Operational recovery
+CommerceControl record 6ad6b6758f2fd61c242969e0 (key commerce-global-v1) is the singleton gate. Do not delete or duplicate it.
+Clean validation failures release it. A failure after the first intended write retains review_required; a terminated worker may leave running. Neither expires automatically because an older worker could still complete a write.
+
+An administrator must inspect action, started_at, affected orders/purchases/reservation markers and ledger entries, reconcile uncertain writes and confirm the old invocation cannot continue before explicitly restoring idle. There is deliberately no automatic unlock/replay endpoint. Do not release a claimed card reservation until the provider confirms the session cannot collect payment.
+
+## Remaining limits
+- This is serialization plus conditional writes, not an all-entity database transaction. Partial writes need reconciliation and can pause commerce.
+- The legacy review-bonus handler and browser dispute-resolution wallet writers still need migration to the shared gate. Do not regard all historical financial writers as transaction-safe.
+- COD collection verification, real courier integration, automatic refunds and mobile-money integrations remain unfinished. No fake successful payments are enabled.
+- Historical orders were not migrated; orders lacking trusted provenance require administrative review.
+- The Base44 editor preview remains blocked by its GitHub connection to michelbuki14/congo-commerce1. Reconnect that integration to validate the complete browser flow. Backend routing was tested independently.
+- No valid external payment or withdrawal transfer was performed. Production credentials, provider success callbacks, scheduled automation and privacy-link routing still require live end-to-end validation.
+- The existing 12 dependency advisories remain.
+
+No Publish or CLI deploy command was run; sandbox backend/entity edits synchronize through Base44. The prior saved restore point was 8a17c2a82825431ffc18e5ebfe8172f0853858a8.
